<title>UK: AEA wins technology order from Railtrack.</title>
<headline>AEA wins technology order from Railtrack.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's AEA Technology Plc said on Tuesday that Railtrack Plc had ordered 3.1 million stg of computerised monitoring equipment designed to help prevent damage to the overhead line equipment on electrified sections of the railway.</p>
<p>The science and nuclear technology company said  the order was placed with its BRR unit, formerly British Rail Research. The system is known as Panchex.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
